<h2>Austin Commercial Roof Repair</h2>
<p>Most of the Austin commercial roof repair calls we take come down to a handful of causes. Large flat roofs collect water and debris, rooftop equipment gets serviced by trades who are not roofers, and Central Texas heat expands and contracts membranes every single day.</p>
<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="feature"><h3>Leaks at penetrations</h3><p>HVAC curbs, pipe stacks, skylights and conduit are where most membrane roofs start leaking. We rebuild flashing and boots rather than smearing mastic over them.</p></div>
  <div class="feature"><h3>Ponding water</h3><p>Water that sits more than 48 hours after rain speeds up membrane aging and adds weight. We clear drains and scuppers and can add crickets or tapered insulation to move water off.</p></div>
  <div class="feature"><h3>Punctures &amp; seam failures</h3><p>Dropped tools, hail and foot traffic open small holes; open seams let water travel under the membrane far from where it shows up inside.</p></div>
  <div class="feature"><h3>Blisters &amp; UV cracking</h3><p>Trapped moisture and years of Texas sun leave bitumen and older membranes cracked and brittle. We repair what is sound and tell you when it is not.</p></div>
</div>
<p>Every repair visit ends with photos and a short written summary, so you have a record for your maintenance file, your insurer or your next budget meeting.</p>

